<article class="env-lemma" id="0CF3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CF3">Lemma <span data-tag="0CF3">37.10.4</span>.</a> Consider a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (X \subset X') \ar[rr]_{(f, f')} \ar[rd] &  &  (Y \subset Y') \ar[ld] \\  &  (S \subset S') }  \]
</div>
  <p> of thickenings. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$Y' \to S'$ is locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X' \to S'$ is flat and locally of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is flat, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X = S \times _{S'} X'$ and $Y = S \times _{S'} Y'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $f'$ is flat and for all $y' \in Y'$ in the image of $f'$ the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{Y', y'}$ is flat and essentially of finite presentation over $\mathcal{O}_{S', s'}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CEL" data-tag="0CEL">10.128.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>